 "title": "ZooMS band pattern (A-E) and its verdict",
 "description": "Six collagen-associated bands (bands.json): protein-type N-H 2044 and amide 2175; the other four (parameter ch_bands, an id): C-H 1689 and 1728, a combination band at 2262 (assignment uncertain; not a clean C-H band) and amide III + CH2 2284, read on the evidence kernel. Lit = E_b > lit_if_E_above. Readable unless sd_E > sd_max_frac_w x w_b and E_b < unreadable_only_if_E_below_frac_w x w_b (sd_E = keyed band gain x N2 of the band's noise window, as measured). Pattern A all flat; B both protein bands flat; C one protein band lit; D both protein lit, another band flat; E all six lit. Verdict: Unlikely = both protein bands readable and flat; Good = all six readable and lit; Borderline = both protein bands readable and either exactly one lit, or both lit with a readable other band flat; Can't tell = anything else. Pattern letters are internal; the UI says it in words. Vote: after the pattern verdict, an Unlikely becomes Borderline when the vote band (the OH-corrected 1545 nm trough) is readable (unless sd_u > sd_max_frac_w and u < unreadable_only_if_E_below_frac_w, in u = u_sign x E / w) and u > lit_if_u_above; Good and Can't tell are unchanged.",
